---
// Interactive blog article: a Day-0 mood board for industrial techno.
// Deliberately standalone (no SiteLayout/Tailwind) to keep the piece's
// own art direction; fonts are self-hosted like the rest of the site.
import "@fontsource-variable/big-shoulders-display";
import "@fontsource-variable/archivo";
import "@fontsource-variable/martian-mono";
import { getImage } from "astro:assets";
import heroSrc from "../../assets/images/blog/triangulation.jpg";

const title = "Triangulation — Max Hodges";
const description =
  "A Day-0 mood board for industrial techno: twelve artists mapped across Pressure, Hypnosis and Atmosphere, sized by a year of listening data.";
const canonical = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site);
const ogImage = new URL(
  (await getImage({ src: heroSrc, width: 1200, format: "jpeg" })).src,
  Astro.site,
).href;
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="article" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Max Hodges" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonical} />
    <meta property="og:image" content={ogImage} />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content={title} />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content={description} />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content={ogImage} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <style is:global>
      :root{
        --bg:#0d1013; --panel:#141a1f; --raise:#1a2128; --fg:#e7e2d6; --muted:#8d959c; --line:#28313a;
        --machine:#d36a40; --loop:#9b8cf2; --space:#47b5aa;
        --display:"Big Shoulders Display Variable", "Arial Narrow", Impact, sans-serif;
        --body:"Archivo Variable", "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
        --mono:"Martian Mono Variable", ui-monospace, "SFMono-Regular", Menlo, monospace;
        color-scheme:dark;
      }
      *,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:border-box}
      html,body{margin:0;padding:0}
      img{max-width:100%}
      body{background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font-family:var(--body);font-size:15px;line-height:1.55}
      .wrap{max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto;padding-left:max(16px, env(safe-area-inset-left, 0px));padding-right:max(16px, env(safe-area-inset-right, 0px));padding-block:28px 64px}
      .sitenav{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:.03em;margin-bottom:26px}
      .sitenav a{color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none}
      .sitenav a:hover{color:var(--fg)}
      .sitenav span{color:var(--line);padding:0 6px}
      .eyebrow{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)}
      h1{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(56px,11vw,128px);line-height:.86;letter-spacing:.01em;margin:8px 0 14px;text-transform:uppercase;text-wrap:balance}
      .lede{max-width:64ch;color:var(--fg);font-size:17px;margin:0}
      .lede b{font-weight:600}
      .main{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.3fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:28px;margin-top:28px;align-items:start}
      @media (max-width:900px){.main{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}}
      .plot{min-width:0}
      .plot svg{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}
      .legend{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px 18px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:18px}
      .legend .hintlabel{color:var(--fg)}
      .legend span{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px}
      .sw{width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:50%;display:inline-block}

      /* threads */
      .threads{margin-top:16px}
      .chips{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin-top:8px}
      .chip{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:.02em;background:var(--panel);color:var(--fg);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:999px;padding:7px 12px;cursor:pointer}
      .chip:hover{border-color:var(--muted)}
      .chip[aria-pressed="true"]{background:var(--fg);color:var(--bg);border-color:var(--fg)}
      .chip:focus-visible,.node:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--fg);outline-offset:3px}
      .threadnote{min-height:3.2em;margin:10px 0 0;color:var(--muted);font-size:14px;max-width:70ch}
      .threadnote b{color:var(--fg);font-weight:600}

      /* svg */
      .ring{fill-opacity:.07;stroke-width:1.5}
      .ringlabel{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:800;font-size:56px;letter-spacing:.04em}
      .ringsub{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:15px;fill:var(--muted)}
      .zonelabel{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:14px;letter-spacing:.14em;fill:var(--muted)}
      .radar{fill:none;stroke:var(--line);stroke-dasharray:2 6}
      .node{cursor:pointer;transition:opacity .25s}
      .node circle.dot{fill:var(--bg);stroke:var(--fg);stroke-width:1.5;transition:fill .2s}
      .node text{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:17px;fill:var(--fg);text-anchor:middle;letter-spacing:.04em}
      .node:hover circle.dot{fill:var(--raise)}
      .node.sel circle.dot{fill:var(--fg)}
      .node.dim{opacity:.16}
      .node .halo{fill:none;stroke:var(--fg);stroke-width:1;opacity:0}
      .node.lit .halo{opacity:.55}
      .you text{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:800;font-size:22px;fill:var(--fg);text-anchor:middle;letter-spacing:.1em}
      .you line{stroke:var(--fg);stroke-width:1.2}
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion:no-preference){
        .node.lit .halo{animation:pulse 2.4s ease-in-out infinite}
        @keyframes pulse{0%,100%{opacity:.15}50%{opacity:.7}}
        /* Until the first interaction, every dot breathes faintly so the
           map reads as tappable. */
        svg.idle .node:not(.sel) .halo{animation:breathe 3.2s ease-in-out infinite}
        @keyframes breathe{0%,100%{opacity:.06}50%{opacity:.35}}
      }

      /* panel */
      .panel{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;padding:22px 22px 18px;min-width:0;position:sticky;top:16px}
      @media (max-width:900px){.panel{position:static}}
      .panel h2{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:800;font-size:46px;line-height:.95;margin:6px 0 4px;text-transform:uppercase}
      .meta{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6}
      .zonepill{display:inline-block;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;margin-top:10px;color:var(--bg)}
      .mins{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;margin-top:12px;color:var(--fg)}
      .mins .bar{height:4px;background:var(--line);border-radius:2px;margin-top:6px;overflow:hidden}
      .mins .bar i{display:block;height:100%;background:var(--fg)}
      .panel .aes{font-size:16px;margin:16px 0 0}
      .panel h3{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);margin:18px 0 6px;font-weight:500}
      .panel ul{margin:0;padding-left:18px;display:grid;gap:5px}
      .try{margin-top:16px;border-left:3px solid var(--fg);padding:10px 12px;background:var(--raise);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0}
      .try p{margin:0}
      .tags{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px;margin-top:4px}
      .tags span{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:3px;padding:2px 7px;color:var(--muted)}
      .src{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}
      .src a{color:var(--fg);text-underline-offset:3px;text-decoration-color:var(--muted)}

      /* reading sections */
      section.read{margin-top:56px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:22px}
      section.read h2{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(34px,5vw,52px);text-transform:uppercase;margin:6px 0 16px;line-height:.95;text-wrap:balance}
      .zones{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(260px,1fr));gap:14px}
      .zone{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;padding:16px;min-width:0}
      .zone h4{margin:0 0 4px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;font-weight:500}
      .zone .who{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:8px}
      .zone p{margin:0;font-size:14px}
      .cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:32px}
      @media (max-width:800px){.cols{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}}
      .prose p{max-width:64ch;margin:0 0 12px}
      ol.recipe{margin:0;padding-left:22px;display:grid;gap:10px;max-width:64ch}
      ol.recipe b{font-weight:600}
      .q{margin-top:18px;font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;font-size:26px;line-height:1.1;max-width:30ch;text-wrap:balance}
      .notes{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);max-width:80ch}
      .keygrid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1.4fr);gap:32px}
      @media (max-width:800px){.keygrid{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}}
      .keylist{display:grid;gap:12px;margin:0}
      .keyrow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:56px minmax(0,1fr);gap:12px;align-items:center}
      .keyrow svg{width:56px;height:40px;display:block}
      .keyrow dt{display:contents}
      .keyrow dd{margin:0;font-size:14px}
      .keyrow dd b{font-weight:600}
      .sizes svg{width:100%;max-width:340px;height:auto;display:block}
      .sizes text{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;fill:var(--muted);text-anchor:middle}
      .gloss{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(240px,1fr));gap:10px 24px;margin:0}
      .gloss div{min-width:0}
      .gloss dt{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--fg)}
      .gloss dd{margin:2px 0 0;font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}
      .notes p{margin:0 0 8px}
      .credit{max-width:72ch;margin:16px 0 0;padding:12px 14px;border-left:2px solid var(--fg);background:var(--panel);color:var(--muted);font-size:14px;border-radius:0 4px 4px 0}
      .credit b{color:var(--fg);font-weight:600}
      .credit a{color:var(--fg);text-underline-offset:3px;text-decoration-color:var(--muted)}
      ol.story{margin:0;padding-left:22px;display:grid;gap:12px;max-width:68ch}
      ol.story b{font-weight:600}
      .madewith{margin-top:16px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}
    </style>

    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="sitenav" aria-label="Site">
        <a href="/">Max Hodges</a><span>/</span><a href="/blog">Projects</a>
      </nav>
      <div class="eyebrow">Day 0 mood board · industrial techno · interactive</div>
      <h1>Triangulation</h1>
      <p class="lede">Three territories run through the artists I study: <b style="color:var(--machine)">Pressure</b> (weight, distortion, noise), <b style="color:var(--loop)">Hypnosis</b> (strict repetition, groove, trance) and <b style="color:var(--space)">Atmosphere</b> (space, sci-fi worlds, sound treated as material). I sit where all three overlap. Tap an artist for a readout, or pick a thread to see who shares it.</p>
      <p class="credit">Inspired by <b>Day 0: Vision &amp; Planning</b> in Oscar Verlinden's <a href="https://courses.underdog.brussels/courses/techno-entire-track-creation" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Industrial Techno: Start to Finish</a> course at Underdog Electronic Music School, Brussels. His point: get clear on what you're making and why before you open the DAW, or the tools lead you into random territory. A mood board collects the key stylistic references and asks which part of each one is crucial to the project. This is mine.</p>

      <div class="main">
        <div class="plot">
          <svg viewBox="0 -50 1000 1090" class="venn idle" role="img" aria-label="Venn diagram of three territories, Pressure, Hypnosis and Atmosphere, with twelve artists placed in their regions and me at the centre">
            <g aria-hidden="true">
              <circle class="radar" cx="500" cy="470" r="90"/>
              <circle class="radar" cx="500" cy="470" r="190"/>
              <circle class="radar" cx="500" cy="470" r="300"/>
              <circle class="radar" cx="500" cy="470" r="420"/>
              <circle class="ring" cx="370" cy="360" r="300" fill="var(--machine)" stroke="var(--machine)"/>
              <circle class="ring" cx="630" cy="360" r="300" fill="var(--loop)" stroke="var(--loop)"/>
              <circle class="ring" cx="500" cy="585" r="300" fill="var(--space)" stroke="var(--space)"/>
              <text class="ringlabel" x="20" y="8" fill="var(--machine)">PRESSURE</text>
              <text class="ringsub" x="22" y="42">distortion · noise · weight</text>
              <text class="ringlabel" x="980" y="8" fill="var(--loop)" text-anchor="end">HYPNOSIS</text>
              <text class="ringsub" x="978" y="42" text-anchor="end">repetition · groove · trance</text>
              <text class="ringlabel" x="500" y="958" fill="var(--space)" text-anchor="middle">ATMOSPHERE</text>
              <text class="ringsub" x="500" y="992" text-anchor="middle">space · sci-fi · sound as material</text>
              <text class="zonelabel" x="505" y="128" text-anchor="middle">RITUAL</text>
              <text class="zonelabel" x="255" y="505" text-anchor="middle">DYSTOPIA</text>
              <text class="zonelabel" x="745" y="505" text-anchor="middle">MEDITATIVE</text>
            </g>
            <g class="you" aria-hidden="true">
              <line x1="470" y1="497" x2="530" y2="497"/><line x1="500" y1="467" x2="500" y2="527"/>
              <circle cx="500" cy="497" r="12" fill="none" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="1.2"/>
              <text x="500" y="562">ME</text>
            </g>
            <g id="nodes"></g>
          </svg>
          <div class="legend">
            <span class="hintlabel">Tap an artist for a readout</span>
            <span><i class="sw" style="background:var(--machine)"></i>Pressure</span>
            <span><i class="sw" style="background:var(--loop)"></i>Hypnosis</span>
            <span><i class="sw" style="background:var(--space)"></i>Atmosphere</span>
            <span>Dot size = my Apple Music Replay minutes, Jan–Sep 2026</span>
          </div>

          <div class="threads">
            <div class="eyebrow">Shared threads</div>
            <div class="chips" id="chips"></div>
            <p class="threadnote" id="threadnote">Each thread cuts across the circles. Pick one to light up the artists who share it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <aside class="panel" id="panel" aria-live="polite"></aside>
      </div>

      <section class="read">
        <div class="eyebrow">How to read the map</div>
        <h2>Three circles, three overlaps, one centre</h2>
        <div class="zones">
          <div class="zone"><h4><i class="sw" style="background:var(--machine)"></i>Pressure</h4><div class="who">Ansome · 93sovage</div><p>Physical weight. Booming or staggered kicks, sheet-noise distortion, one-note subs, rave stabs, noise played as texture. Hardware and modular first, little melody. Atonal and harsh in timbre, but rarely dissonant in the harmonic sense.</p></div>
          <div class="zone"><h4><i class="sw" style="background:var(--loop)"></i>Hypnosis</h4><div class="who">Truncate · Developer</div><p>Tracks as tools. A few layers built to be mixed, jacking Chicago or tunnel-like warehouse grooves, numbered rather than named.</p></div>
          <div class="zone"><h4><i class="sw" style="background:var(--space)"></i>Atmosphere</h4><div class="who">Kangding Ray</div><p>Sound as architecture. Granular texture, broken uneven rhythm, emotional and cinematic, built mostly by taking things away.</p></div>
          <div class="zone"><h4>Ritual · Pressure × Hypnosis</h4><div class="who">Regis · Surgeon</div><p>The Birmingham method: strict sequences, no breakdowns or fills, a mantra built from layered percussion and dub space.</p></div>
          <div class="zone"><h4>Dystopia · Pressure × Atmosphere</h4><div class="who">Tommy Four Seven · Scalameriya · Headless Horseman</div><p>Sci-fi, horror and gothic worlds over broken, syncopated drums. All three have released on Tommy Four Seven's 47 label, and VSK has too.</p></div>
          <div class="zone"><h4>Meditative · Hypnosis × Atmosphere</h4><div class="who">Dotdat</div><p>One motif held for the whole track while drums and noise shift around it. Heavy but meditative, Detroit-leaning groove.</p></div>
          <div class="zone"><h4>Centre · all three</h4><div class="who">VSK · me</div><p>VSK sits closest to me: hard industrial on one side, "mental" hypnotic tracks on the other, cosmology in the titles. What all twelve share is the brief my notes keep circling: few elements, short sounds, change by subtraction, and processing that turns a plain source into a character.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="read">
        <div class="eyebrow">My plan</div>
        <h2>Start in the Hypnosis circle, make tools</h2>
        <div class="cols">
          <div class="prose">
            <p>My sticking point is development: I get a loop going and stall on how to grow it into a track. Minimal techno doesn't remove development. It moves it out of the arrangement and into mutes, filter moves, effect sends and velocity. That suits a modular rig and the "mute, don't edit" rule I wrote down after studying Kone.</p>
            <p>A <b>DJ tool</b> is a track made to be used inside a DJ set instead of listened to on its own. It's a working loop with a long, stable groove, mostly drums and one or two elements, that a DJ layers on top of another record for a few minutes. It has no real intro, no story and no big drop, and on its own it can sound almost unfinished. That's intentional.</p>
            <p>Truncate and Developer get around the problem by not making songs. Truncate began as numbered DJ tools and keeps tracks "simple and not too complicated". Developer's <i>In Pure Form</i> is 25 numbered tracks billed as no-filler tools. A tool doesn't need a story. It needs to hold a dancefloor for six minutes while someone mixes it.</p>
            <p>So "how do I develop this?" gets a smaller answer: I don't, past four or five mute moves. I'll number the tracks instead of naming them, so none of them has to be the important one.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <ol class="recipe">
              <li><b>Kick plus a VSK tail.</b> Dry kick, plus a send through delay, distortion and reverb on the matrix mixer, pitched slightly and blended low so it swells and recedes.</li>
              <li><b>Toms from the kick.</b> The same kick voice, pitched up per step from Hermod+, random velocity, two hits pushed late, a stereo delay to glue them. This is VSK's method, as he teaches it in his Home of Sound course.</li>
              <li><b>One motif.</b> A short stab or acid figure. Never change the notes, only the filter and the sends (Dotdat).</li>
              <li><b>One space layer.</b> A drone or a resampled effects return sitting under the kick (Kangding Ray, Tommy Four Seven).</li>
              <li><b>Arrange by muting.</b> Record a 7-minute pass into Bitwig with four mute moves and no breakdown (Regis). Export the same day as Tool 01.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="q">Which part will I want to keep "developing", and what happens if I leave it as a tool?</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="read" id="legend">
        <div class="eyebrow">Legend</div>
        <h2>Key and terms</h2>
        <div class="keygrid">
          <div>
            <dl class="keylist">
              <div class="keyrow"><dt><svg viewBox="0 0 56 40" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="28" cy="20" r="17" fill="var(--machine)" fill-opacity=".12" stroke="var(--machine)" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></dt><dd><b style="color:var(--machine)">Pressure</b>: weight, distortion, noise. Physical force from the kick and sub.</dd></div>
              <div class="keyrow"><dt><svg viewBox="0 0 56 40" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="28" cy="20" r="17" fill="var(--loop)" fill-opacity=".12" stroke="var(--loop)" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></dt><dd><b style="color:var(--loop)">Hypnosis</b>: strict repetition and groove that pulls you into a trance.</dd></div>
              <div class="keyrow"><dt><svg viewBox="0 0 56 40" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="28" cy="20" r="17" fill="var(--space)" fill-opacity=".12" stroke="var(--space)" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></dt><dd><b style="color:var(--space)">Atmosphere</b>: space, sci-fi worlds, sound treated as a material.</dd></div>
              <div class="keyrow"><dt><svg viewBox="0 0 56 40" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="20" cy="20" r="14" fill="var(--machine)" fill-opacity=".14" stroke="var(--machine)" stroke-width="1.2"/><circle cx="36" cy="20" r="14" fill="var(--loop)" fill-opacity=".14" stroke="var(--loop)" stroke-width="1.2"/></svg></dt><dd><b>Overlaps</b>: Ritual (Pressure × Hypnosis), Dystopia (Pressure × Atmosphere), Meditative (Hypnosis × Atmosphere).</dd></div>
              <div class="keyrow"><dt><svg viewBox="0 0 56 40" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="14" y1="20" x2="42" y2="20" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="1.2"/><line x1="28" y1="6" x2="28" y2="34" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="1.2"/><circle cx="28" cy="20" r="7" fill="none" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="1.2"/></svg></dt><dd><b>Me</b>: the point where all three circles meet.</dd></div>
              <div class="keyrow"><dt><svg viewBox="0 0 56 40" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="28" cy="20" r="11" fill="var(--bg)" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></dt><dd><b>Artist</b>: tap it for a readout.</dd></div>
              <div class="keyrow"><dt><svg viewBox="0 0 56 40" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="28" cy="20" r="11" fill="var(--fg)" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></dt><dd><b>Filled</b>: the artist shown in the readout.</dd></div>
              <div class="keyrow"><dt><svg viewBox="0 0 56 40" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="28" cy="20" r="17" fill="none" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="1" opacity=".6"/><circle cx="28" cy="20" r="11" fill="var(--bg)" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></dt><dd><b>Ring</b>: shares the thread you picked. Faded dots don't.</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <div class="sizes" style="margin-top:20px">
              <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:6px">Dot size · my 2026 listening minutes</div>
              <svg viewBox="0 0 340 96" aria-label="Dot sizes for 100, 500, 1,000 and 2,500 minutes">
                <circle cx="30" cy="42" r="11.9" fill="var(--bg)" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="1.2"/><text x="30" y="90">100</text>
                <circle cx="100" cy="42" r="17.4" fill="var(--bg)" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="1.2"/><text x="100" y="90">500</text>
                <circle cx="180" cy="42" r="21.6" fill="var(--bg)" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="1.2"/><text x="180" y="90">1,000</text>
                <circle cx="280" cy="42" r="33.3" fill="var(--bg)" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="1.2"/><text x="280" y="90">2,500</text>
              </svg>
            </div>
          </div>
          <dl class="gloss">
            <div><dt>DJ tool</dt><dd>A track built to be mixed inside a set: a long, steady groove with few elements and no story. Done when the groove holds.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Motif</dt><dd>One short figure, stab or note repeated for the whole track instead of a melody that develops.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Atonal</dt><dd>No key centre. Different from dissonant, which means clashing pitches.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Broken beat</dt><dd>Syncopated percussion off the straight 4/4 grid. In this scene it mostly comes from UK bass, jungle and drum &amp; bass.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Kick tail</dt><dd>VSK's rumble: the dry kick plus a delayed, distorted, reverbed copy blended low so it swells and recedes.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Dub space</dt><dd>Delay and reverb sends played live, so the echoes become part of the arrangement.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Resampling</dt><dd>Recording your own output, such as an effects return, back as audio and cutting it into a new part.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Granular</dt><dd>Chopping a sound into tiny grains and rearranging them into textures, for example with a Morphagene.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Hard mute vs fade</dt><dd>A hard mute on a phrase boundary punctuates. A fade or filter ride evolves.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>HPF roll-off</dt><dd>Sweeping a high-pass filter up so the kick thins out without disappearing. A DJ move that works in arrangements too.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>47 · Perc Trax · Downwards</dt><dd>Labels that link these artists: Tommy Four Seven's 47, Perc's Perc Trax, and Regis's Downwards.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Threads</dt><dd>Traits that cut across the circles. Pick one under the diagram to light up who shares it.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="read">
        <div class="eyebrow">Create your own</div>
        <h2>How I made this</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>I started by giving Claude Code three sources of data on my listening. The first was my music journal. I've kept it for a couple of years to plan and reflect on studio sessions, and to take active-listening notes on tracks by artists I admire, ranging from quick-reference entries to fully charted analyses.</p>
          <p>The second was my Apple Music library. In the Music app on the Mac, File → Library → Export Library… saves an XML file listing every track I've saved, with its play count, skip count, and last-played date. Mine held about 7,600 tracks going back to 2004.</p>
          <p>The third was Apple Music Replay at music.apple.com/replay. It shows top artists, songs, and albums for each month, with minutes listened, and it counts streams of tracks I never saved, which the library export misses. Claude extracted and analyzed the data month by month from January to September 2026.</p>
          <p>The sources told different stories. The library export reflects years of habit, with Download, Phil Western and Kangding Ray near the top. Replay showed what I'm studying now: VSK at over 2,600 minutes for the year, then Dotdat, Regis, and Scalameriya, who appears in every month.</p>
          <p>Then I asked Claude Code to make a mood board by finding the themes my favorite artists share. I suggested something like a Venn diagram with me in the middle, but left it free to choose the visualization. To find the themes, it researched each artist through reviews, interviews, and label pages, placed them into three overlapping territories, and sized each dot based on my listening. From there, we refined it together.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="madewith">Built in conversation with Claude, October 2026.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="read notes">
        <div class="eyebrow">Notes on the data</div>
        <p>Minutes are lower bounds from Apple Music Replay, January to September 2026. Each month only shows its top 14 to 20 artists. Truncate's figure leaves out his joint tracks with Dotdat. 93sovage's minutes are all from June and July.</p>
        <p>93sovage has no reviews; his profile comes from a radio-show bio and an event listing.</p>
        <p>Profiles summarise reviews and interviews linked in each readout. Dotdat has only bios and event listings, no proper reviews. Scalameriya has no documented gear or process. VSK's tom and kick-tail technique comes from my notes on his Home of Sound course, not from press.</p>
        <p>Corrections found along the way: Ansome is Kieran Whitefield. Developer is Adrian Sandoval. VSK's Polarization LP came out on Warm Up, not 47. "Colony" is a track on Tommy Four Seven's Veer.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

